Subject: [PATCH] v8: build heap.cc and local-heap.cc at -O0 for mipsel

V8 dropped the MIPS port in 2019 and the unmaintained mips32 code
stops working with GCC 16 codegen under qemu-mipsel. mksnapshot
crashes during snapshot bootstrap with:

  # Fatal error in , line 0
  # Check failed: old_state.IsRunning().

The check sits on a std::atomic<ThreadState> compare_exchange in
LocalHeap. Root cause is not fully isolated; likely candidates are
GCC 16 atomic codegen for mips32 or qemu-mipsel LL/SC emulation of
the resulting instruction sequence. Narrowing individual -fno-*
flags (tree-fre, tree-dse, ipa-modref, ipa-pure-const, tree-pta)
did not eliminate the crash; only -O0 on the two files that own the
LocalHeap transitions does.

This patch lowers optimization to -O0 just for heap.cc and
local-heap.cc on mipsel. Cost: a few extra seconds of mksnapshot
runtime under qemu, no runtime impact on the produced node binary
(snapshot is data).

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [legacy mips32 + abandoned V8 port]

--- a/deps/v8/src/heap/heap.cc
+++ b/deps/v8/src/heap/heap.cc
@@ -2,6 +2,9 @@
 // Use of this source code is governed by a BSD-style license that can be
 // found in the LICENSE file.

+// GCC 16 + qemu-mipsel workaround: build at -O0 to avoid mksnapshot crash.
+#pragma GCC optimize("O0")
+
 #include "src/heap/heap.h"

 #include <atomic>
--- a/deps/v8/src/heap/local-heap.cc
+++ b/deps/v8/src/heap/local-heap.cc
@@ -2,6 +2,9 @@
 // Use of this source code is governed by a BSD-style license that can be
 // found in the LICENSE file.

+// GCC 16 + qemu-mipsel workaround: build at -O0 to avoid mksnapshot crash.
+#pragma GCC optimize("O0")
+
 #include "src/heap/local-heap.h"

 #include <atomic>
